====================================================
DESIGN DIRECTION
====================================================

Make the UI clean, premium, simple, and calm.
Use a professional construction SaaS feel.
Avoid clutter.
Avoid heavy enterprise-style screens.
Use whitespace, clear hierarchy, soft cards, subtle dividers, and calm status colors.

Preferred app navigation style:
Use a HouzzPro-inspired layout:
- dark compact main left navigation
- clear active states
- white secondary sidebar for project/company/settings sections when needed
- tree-style secondary navigation for grouped sections
- compact spacing with breathing room
- no cluttered badges in sidebars
- direct landing into useful sections instead of generic overview cards

For tables:
- headers can be bold
- badges/buttons can be emphasized
- normal row cell text should not be overly bold
- avoid dense, hard-to-scan tables when cards would work better on mobile

Mobile:
The MVP is web-first, but it must work well on mobile browser.
Make pages responsive.
No tiny tables on mobile.
Use cards, stacked layouts, large tap targets, and simple upload/update actions.

====================================================
ROLE SAFETY
====================================================

Always respect role-based access.

Roles include:
- CONVAZANT Super Admin
- DECKARC Admin / Company Admin
- GC / Project Manager
- Subcontractor
- Client / Homeowner

Client/Homeowner users should only see client-safe information.

Never expose the following to clients unless explicitly marked client-visible:
- internal admin notes
- internal GC/sub notes
- internal financials
- internal operational records
- private permit/inspection notes
- internal files/photos

Client Portal Preview:
- must remain read-only for risky actions
- must not switch Supabase auth user
- can show the client experience safely
- must not allow upload, delete, payment actions, message sends, or edits unless explicitly requested

====================================================
PROJECT AND CLIENT RULES
====================================================

Projects should be separate records.

A client can have multiple linked projects through project_users.

For client users:
- if linkedProjects.length === 1, open that project directly
- if linkedProjects.length > 1, show My Projects
- if linkedProjects.length === 0, show a safe empty state

Do not merge multiple projects into one record.
Do not create parent/child project structures unless explicitly requested.

Admin Projects list:
Separate project rows are correct.
If needed, create a View by Client grouping UI, but keep each project as its own record.

Add Another Project for This Client:
When creating another project for the same client:
- create a clean separate project record
- link it to the same CLIENT user through project_users
- normalize client email using trim().toLowerCase()
- prefill client details
- prefill current project property/address/location details
- keep all property/address fields editable
- save form values, not blindly copied values
- do not create duplicate client users
- do not create duplicate project_users links

Do not copy old operational records into the new project:
- tasks
- milestones
- permits
- inspections
- files
- photos
- messages
- selections
- payments
- schedule impacts
- daily updates
- action items
- materials
- checklist items

====================================================
LIVE OPERATIONS RULES
====================================================

Operational dashboards should exclude:
- deleted projects
- archived projects
- completed projects

unless the page is specifically for history/archive/deleted records.

Permit/inspection logic should respect permit applicability:
- Applicable
- Not Applicable
- To Be Confirmed

If permits are Not Applicable:
- do not show false permit blockers
- do not create live operations alerts for permit issues
- preserve existing records safely if any exist

Tomorrow’s Plan and ProjectPulse should focus on:
- tasks starting tomorrow
- tasks due tomorrow
- tasks continuing tomorrow
- schedule impacts affecting tomorrow
- crew/material readiness
- scheduled inspections
- blockers and urgent items

ProjectPulse should reflect active Action Board states:
- active items = not Done and not snoozed
- resolved items = Done
- do not show red critical styling when active count is zero

====================================================
FILE / DOCUMENT RULES
====================================================

Before save/upload:
Selected files are temporary and must be removable before upload.
If a user accidentally selects the same file twice, show a duplicate warning.
Only upload files still in the queue when Save/Upload is clicked.

After save/upload:
Files should be managed records with:
- View
- Download
- Delete, based on role permissions
- uploaded date/time
- uploaded by
- user role if available
- visibility badge if applicable

Use role-safe permissions:
- Admin can manage project files
- GC can manage allowed project files
- Subcontractor can usually delete only their own uploads
- Client can only see client-visible files and delete only allowed own uploads
- Client Portal Preview must not allow upload/delete

Do not expose internal-only files to clients.

Use soft delete if supported:
- is_deleted
- deleted_at
- deleted_by

Do not physically delete from storage unless the existing app pattern already does this safely.

